{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559435-mage-scarlett-dawns-a-post-apocalyptic-setting-for-mage-and-changeling","id":1559435,"title":"Mage: Scarlett Dawns (A Post-Apocalyptic setting for Mage and Changeling)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-15T14:47:20-07:00","id":1559435,"title":"Mage: Scarlett Dawns (A Post-Apocalyptic setting for Mage and Changeling)","content":"The subtitle refers to civilization slowly restarting after a century of plagues and terror. (&quot;Red in the Morning/ Sailor's warning) This is a different Ascension War. A modified form of Smallpox came out of Russia in the later 2030s and wiped out billions in a few months. Vampires, (both Cainite and Cathayan), Wraiths, Risen, all being dead were unaffected by the disease organism. Ghouls, Dampir, and Mummies of various types were also immune. All Fera and Kinfolk, all Changelings and Kinane, and similar fay related folk were also immune. Why isn't clear. All Mages, Sorcerers, Psions, and anyone using numia, were also immune. Similarly, no one understands why. Theories are all over the place.<br /> <br /> With the planetary population plunging from around eight billion to 500 million in less than a year the Umbra went insane for decades. However, both Paradox and Banality seemed to be jamed in some way. Bedlam replaced Banality as the main threat to Changelings. Mages were often able to create areas of refuge and stability because of radically reduced Paradox and the lower population providing less resistance to magic.<br /> <br /> Over time communities stabilized. The modified Smallpox kept returning and it both deformed and sterilized most survivors. But in spite of that some children kept being born. So communities kept on going.<br /> <br /> Now in the 2180s there hasn't been a visitation of the plague in sixty years. The Shadow Lands feel nearer across a weaker Veil. But Specters and Wraiths no longer make all the world a nightmare. Vampires and their servants still roam. But most Vampires are in topor. Though the few active ones are hungry. Bedlam and Banality have faded. But Glamor is rare too.<br /> <br /> Most human communities are Mage led. These communities are like Crocus blossoms. The first flowers of spring in constant danger from frost.<br /> <br /> #############################<br /> <br /> More later. This setting is mainly Mage.<br /> <br /> Please free free to Kibbitze. I might use your ideas or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-22-2026, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T06:18:48-07:00","id":1559453,"title":"","content":"This likely isn't too relevant for Mage, but those Wraiths that died from the black plague showed up with unique death marks and in enough numbers to change the entire demographic. That likely happened with this Pox. If there's a supernatural component to the disease that may also have carried over in some way.<br /> <br /> For Mage, the reduced population may have done away with Paradox in general, or at least dropped it back to the Scourge from Sorcerer's Crusade, where it makes magic unpredictable rather than punishes it.<br /> <br /> Also for Mage, did any of the human populations in Horizon realms get hit by the plague? If not then there's likely a similar number of people being born in Horizon realms as being born on Earth and a large chunk of current mages grew up there. If, on the other hand, they did get hit, likely most of the Horizon realms fell. Strictly speaking they would mostly have faded away or merged with other realms, but I think it would be rather compelling if there are ruins of the various Horizon Realms where pieces of them physically fell down to Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T16:37:25-07:00","id":1559470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559435-mage-scarlett-dawns-a-post-apocalyptic-setting-for-mage-and-changeling?p=1559453#post1559453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This likely isn't too relevant for Mage, but those Wraiths that died from the black plague showed up with unique death marks and in enough numbers to change the entire demographic. That likely happened with this Pox. If there's a supernatural component to the disease that may also have carried over in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea and relevant. I was thinking about the role guhls play in actual Arab folklore. Wraiths are seriously messed up by the chaos caused by the plagues. The barriers between the shadow lands and the skin lands are weaker. Wraiths and Specters are more of a threat. Even Wraiths who aren't malevolent need pathos. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Mage, the reduced population may have done away with Paradox in general, or at least dropped it back to the Scourge from Sorcerer's Crusade, where it makes magic unpredictable rather than punishes it. </div> </div> </div>Paradox is far weaker. However there are REALITY ZONES where the local rules are stronger. <br /> <br /> Also, the population got down to about eighty million people. It's up to around 120 million people planet wide. According to older Mage books it takes less effort to perform magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also for Mage, did any of the human populations in Horizon realms get hit by the plague? If not then there's likely a similar number of people being born in Horizon realms as being born on Earth and a large chunk of current mages grew up there. If, on the other hand, they did get hit, likely most of the Horizon realms fell. Strictly speaking they would mostly have faded away or merged with other realms, but I think it would be rather compelling if there are ruins of the various Horizon Realms where pieces of them physically fell down to Earth. </div> </div> </div>I have not thought about that yet. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T16:58:15-07:00","id":1559471,"title":"","content":"We'll start with some basics. The plague was a modified form of Smallpox that first appeared in areas were Russian troops were fighting to hold on to Tatarstand and Chechnya. It soon spread into Southwestern and South Asia. As the modified Smallpox always took the form of the Black Pox ( a moderately rare form of Smallpox that kills far more quickly and brutally, you rot alive) it wasn't identified as Smallpox for awhile.<br /> <br /> Areas physically remote from Eurasia or Africa had longer to plan how to combat the plague. Mages and some other Supernaturals managed to create islands of safety. Thus, in the 2140s most surviving humans live in places like the Americas, Australia, New Zealand, the British Isles, Japan, and islands generally.<br /> <br /> #####################################<br /> <br /> The plagues brutally weeded out humanity. A group of Hermetics and Etherites came up with a means to modify human genetics to enhance survival. All surviving humans born since the 2080s are genetically modified.<br /> <br /> When creating a character under the age of eighty automatically add a bonus dot to <b>Stamina.</b> Also add one additional bonus dot to each of the three categories <b>Physical, Social </b>and <b>Mental. </b>Note, taking an Attribute above six still requires a <b>Merit.</b> However, two Attributes can be taken above six by taking a merit instead of one.<br /> <br /> Although Mages have high willpower (or they wouldn't be Mages) non Mages born after the 2040s get a bonus point in Willpower. This represents the kind of mindsets it takes to survive this world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-22-2026, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T08:34:18-07:00","id":1559481,"title":"","content":"Each of the major Mage factions shattered. The <b>Technocracy </b>and the <b>Disparate Alliance </b>are gone. But they've left legacies. The <b>Council of the Traditions </b>is still around in a less unified form.<br /> <br /> The present form of the Council is based around an Alliance of the Hermetic Order, the Etherites, and the Mercurial Elites. The Hermetics also maintain their traditional ties to both the Euthanatos and the Sahajiya and has formed the five groups into the basis of the new Council. The Akashayana are pragmatically friendly to the council. They are more semialigned than part of the Council. The Celestial Chorus is similar but less friendly. The Verbena and the Kha'vadi are on speaking terms with the Council. The Kha'vadi tends to let local tribal issues and needs determine the relationship. The Verbena see the Council as going off in the wrong direction but neither useless nor people they want trouble with. <br /> <br /> The Council's main goals are the rebuilding of human society. The Hermetics have set up the <b>Adocentyn Foundation. </b>The name comes from a Hermetic Utopia in the book the Picitrix. The five core members of the Council are working to build a functional model for a new civilization. Democracy, Equality, Community, Education, and Enlightenment are supposed to be the foundations. Different communities seek different ways to make these ideals work. They trade information about both failures and successes. <br /> <br /> More later...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-17-2026, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T09:16:38-07:00","id":1559483,"title":"","content":"On the Horizon Realms stuff, if the Avatar Storm happened, that could have taken care of that element. It may be a good way to simplify the setting to one focused more on islands of safety on Earth, even if the Storm itself it's not a thing anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T18:43:12-07:00","id":1559511,"title":"","content":"Making a note of the name Pisistratus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T18:46:47-07:00","id":1559512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559435-mage-scarlett-dawns-a-post-apocalyptic-setting-for-mage-and-changeling?p=1559483#post1559483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Horizon Realms stuff, if the Avatar Storm happened, that could have taken care of that element. It may be a good way to simplify the setting to one focused more on islands of safety on Earth, even if the Storm itself it's not a thing anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. <br /> <br /> I think some of the Horizon realms will have survived. Some brought to earth for the dramatic possibilities (though I will have to come up with a descent in game reason). Others will have the role of Space Colonists seeking <b>The Earth that Was!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-21T14:56:21-07:00","id":1559551,"title":"","content":"The members of the <b>Council </b>have all transformed.<br /> <br /> <b>The Order of Hermes</b> is strongly focused on society. Their goal is a better society that can rebuild the world better than it was. Education is vital but building functional communities is the goal. Utopia, the perfect society, is seen as a wish dream humanity might achieve thousands of years in the future. It's more important to focus on function than perfection.<br /> <br /> <b>The Etherites </b>seem the least changed but they're actually focused on the nuts and bolts of how societies survive. They come up with power sources, improved crops, functional robots, and the like. They create the material basis of society.<br /> <br /> <b>The Mercurial Elites </b>still value computer and numbers but they were always about communication. News services, shipping, travel and the like are their fields.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sahajiya </b>still about Ananda the sacred pulse of creation. So they're still using the arts and celebrition to connect the Sleepers to Ananda.<br /> <br /> <b>The Chakravanti </b>tend to focus more on <br /> teaching about living a life worth living than on their darker side. However helping to make sure the evils of the older world stay dead is a major goal.<br /> <br /> <b>The Akashayana </b>aren't as closely tied to the <b>Council </b>as they were but, paradoxparadoxically, that makes them vital. The <b>Akashayana </b>run what are basically Buddhist monasteries ( well, they represent a variety of faiths) near but not always associated with <b>Council </b>bases and communities.<br /> <br /> The <b>Verbena, </b>the <b>Celestial Chorus, </b>\u200band the <b>Kha'vadi </b>are more distantly connected to the <b>Council. </b>They form their own communities more isolated from the main <b>Council </b>communities. These communities focus on religion and the cultures that support them. However the main <b>Council </b>communities are vital to supporting these communities so they say connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-10-2026, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T15:55:09-07:00","id":1559574,"title":"","content":"<b>The Disparate Alliance </b>collapsed during the plagues but most of the alliance members are still around. Diminished and weaker but around.<br /> <br /> <b>The Children of Knowledge </b>are a craft that exists mainly within various members of the <b>Council of the Traditions. </b>The alchemists are mainly members of the <b>Etherites </b>and the <b>Hermetics. </b>They have their own cabals within each tradition acting alternately as members of the larger traditions or a seperate tradition according to the circumstances. In the few actual cities (New York, San Francisco, New Orleans) there are independent alchemist groups.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bata'a </b>they are around. In the inhabited Caribbean islands they are a functioning craft. In most of North America the <b>Bata'a </b>function as a faction of the most sympathetic local tradition.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sisters of Hippolyta </b>like the <b>Celestial Chorus, </b>the <b>Kha'vadi </b>and the <b>Verbena, </b>the Sisters form their own communities. The <b>Council </b>is friendly and supportive enough. The Sisters aren't happy but they find the situation tolerable. The Sisters are very willing to cooperate with the hospitals run by the <b>Council </b>or their individual members. In some ways the Sisters have taken the place in society Nuns held between the 1920s and the 1990s.<br /> <br /> <b>Ahl-i-Batin </b>were hit brutally by the plague. The lands in the web of Faith were almost completely empty. The present population of these lands is lower than at any time since before the earliest founding of Jerico or G\u00f6bekli Tepe. The <b>Batini </b>actually have their strongest numbers in the British Isles. In North America the <b>Batini </b>pass themselves off as orphan mages.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kahu </b>are mainly in the Pacific Islands including New Zealand. Australia and California also have groups of these Kahunnas. They maintain trade relationships with the <b>Mercurial Elites.</b> They don't intend to be caught by surprise again.<br /> <br /> <b>The Wu-Lung </b>have their strongholds in Taiwan and the Pacific Islands. However, as the Chinese American community was all over North America the <b>Wu-Lung </b>can be found anywhere. They often join the most sympathetic local cabal.<br /> <br /> <b>The Knights of the Temple of Solomon </b>are basically allies of the <b>Celestial Chorus. </b>The knights stay separate but they find the alliance useful. The knights are becoming more willing to work with the <b>Council</b>. Most of the knights core values remain the same, but pragmatism counts too. <br /> <br /> <b>The Ngoma </b>Africa was brutalized by the plagues. The <b>Ngoma </b>are struggling to rebuild. The <b>Council </b>can't provide much aid but between enhanced crops and medical aid it is seriously helping the situation. The main <b>Ngoma </b>presence in North America is <b>House Ngoma </b>in the <b>Order of Hermes. </b><br /> <br /> <b>The Taftani </b>pretty much went back to their ancient ways just with a vague understanding that they will try not to cause too much chaos. So far the bloodshed is minimal. <br /> <br /> <b>The Hollow Ones </b>don't really exist much. In the few surviving cities of North America there are groups that are orphan mages that live bohemian lifestyles and seem rather morbid. But the popular culture and urban society that gave the <b>Hollow Ones </b>their context are gone. However, people say crows return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-22-2026, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T13:24:07-07:00","id":1559586,"title":"","content":"<b>The Technocratic Union </b>took a harder hit.<br /> <br /> <b>ItX </b>exists only as a faction within <b>The Children of Ether.</b> They still have some distinctive features, but they aren't going to be a major force soon.<br /> <br /> <b>The Progenitors </b>are somewhat more independent. They exist as factions among the <b>Etherites, </b>the <b>Hermetics, </b>and the <b>Mercurial Elites. </b>The non <b>Etherite</b> factions are mainly medical auxiliaries. There are a few <b>Progenitor </b>hospitals in the larger cities. These institutions either perform elective surgeries and biomods or work to maintain the public health. The second function is financed by the first.<br /> <br /> <b>The Void Engineers </b>are the strongest survivors. They still have space bases and patrol the solar system. They are looking to join the <b>Council.</b> The majority of the <b>Traditions </b>favor this, but politics are still in the way.<br /> <br /> <b>The Syndicate </b>and <b>NWO </b>are joined together as the <b>Pisistratus League.</b> Pisistratus was a respected ruler in ancient Greece who had the title of &quot;Tyrant.&quot; He was not &quot;tyrannical&quot; in the modern sense. Basically, the <b>League </b>promotes authoritarian government as the path to rebuilding the world. They aren't having much luck in persuading people. However, the <b>Syndicate </b>does money lending and banks. While the <b>NWO </b>sells &quot;services&quot; to various governments. They make money and have influence. They aren't respected. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-23-2026, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T05:57:28-07:00","id":1559597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559435-mage-scarlett-dawns-a-post-apocalyptic-setting-for-mage-and-changeling?p=1559551#post1559551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Mercurial Elites </b>still value computer and numbers but they were always about communication. News services, shipping, travel and the like are their fields.</div> </div> </div> </div>One interesting aspect could be to explore how the communication networks were hit by the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that with the collapse of society as we know it, Internet fell. The Web went dark. And now the Mercurials are going to be focused on trying to rebuild comunication between the oases of civilization. On a more dangerous world, that means protecting the satelites/cables , which could spark the necessity of a strong collaboration with the Void Engineers even more so than with the other Traditions.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T14:21:58-07:00","id":1559607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559435-mage-scarlett-dawns-a-post-apocalyptic-setting-for-mage-and-changeling?p=1559597#post1559597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One interesting aspect could be to explore how the communication networks were hit by the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I would imagine that with the collapse of society as we know it, Internet fell. The Web went dark. And now the Mercurials are going to be focused on trying to rebuild comunication between the oases of civilization. On a more dangerous world, that means protecting the satelites/cables , which could spark the necessity of a strong collaboration with the Void Engineers even more so than with the other Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are insightful and spotted a key part of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T15:10:03-07:00","id":1559608,"title":"","content":"Since the <b>Council of the Traditions </b>is very out in the open and using the <b>Adocentyn Foundation </b>to promote useful ideals among the populace, it would be useful to mention something of the shape of these ideals. Although no RPG is going to risk a series of philosophy lectures (at least not if you want your gaming group to ever speak to you again) I think you might get them to read three comic books, or rather a graphic novel three comic books long with plenty of jokes.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about <b>Bloke's Progress. </b>Basically, it introduces the reader to the core ideas of <b>John Ruskin. </b>Kevin Jackson wrote an easy and entertaining intro to the ideas of a serious thinker. Ruskin's humane and wise worldviews should give the setting depth. Blend freely with Oscar Wilde's <b>The Soul of Man Under Socialism</b> and the writings of Ben Franklin, Tom Paine, Rosa Luxembourg, Marx, Michael Harrington and MLK.<br /> <br /> Although the <b>Adocentyn Foundation </b>uses markets and certain aspects of Capitalism the ruthlessness of Capitalism is rejected. The strongly stress the democracy in Social Democracy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-24-2026, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T11:39:59-07:00","id":1559618,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampires </b><br /> <br /> Both <b>\u200bCainite </b>and <b>Cathayan </b>vampires were slammed hard by the plague. For western vampires the food supply vanished, well except for ghouls and other vampires. <br /> <br /> There is no known example of a Ghoul surviving the plague. Either they were devoured, died of excellerated aging, or they escaped, broke the bonds of blood became fully human again and probably died of the plague. While it's possible one or two ghouls did survive, it's not something anyone has heard of. Revenants on the other hand make it through. All four families known to the general Sabbat, the three families known to the Inner Hand of the Black Hand, and the families that serve the Tremere (1) and the Baali (2). (Note: I think I missed a few Revenant families). However, not all of the Revenant families were stable enough to survive all that well. The Revenants are alive, but many are in poor condition. The Dampir are surviving as well. Given their advantages and tendency to be more or less sane, assume that they are doing relatively well. <br /> <br /> The <b>Cainites </b>are much rarer and far less powerful in this setting. Although the few neonate vampires that get created are of higher generation and trained by powerful elders, the collapse of human civilization and the loss of the resources that the elder vampires controled stripped the Vampires as a group of power. While individually powerful vampires now lack the means to manipulate from the shadows. The Masquerade is gone, the strings to pull are gone, the wealth that controlled the humans used as herds is gone. What remains are small gangs of predators working as packs to survive while their instincts scream that they are solitary hunters. <br /> <br /> At first the <b>Cathayans </b>laughed. The fall of humanity only took away one source of Chi. However it was soon understood that humans and their communities were the primary source of Chi. As the <b>Cathayans </b>grew weak the <b>Beast Courts </b>and the <b>Hisen</b> both came to understand that if the <b>Cathayans </b>survived the local humans might not. Humans, troublesome as they are, were chosen. The <b>Cathayans </b>were driven out of Asia. The broken remnants of the <b>Cathayan </b>vampires made their way to the Americas to find survival. <br /> <br /> More later...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T13:46:52-07:00","id":1559871,"title":"","content":"<b>Cathayan </b>vampires went to the port cities and resorts of the Pacific Coast of North America and found them deserted or nearly so. The <b>Cathayan </b>vampires mainly went south from Tijuana down to Santiago Chile the Chinese Vampires continue their existence. In South Asia and Maritime Southeast Asia <b>Cathayan </b>vampires still hold on, but in seriously reduced numbers. <br /> <br /> Attempts by <b>Cathayan </b>vampires to invade areas of the Americas beyond their strongholds is a continuous threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-10-2026, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T13:53:14-07:00","id":1559872,"title":"","content":"The <b>Fera </b>are in a much stronger position on this depopulated Earth but they can't reinstate the <b>Impergium.</b> Gaia has managed to communicate the simple fact that destroying humanity would severely damage her. The plagues wounded her severely. Humans must restore themselves and learn to live in peace with nature. And the <b>\u200bFera </b>need to guide not murder them. Gaia also said that <b>Mages </b>are an important part of humanity's destiny. <br /> <br /> The different factions of <b>Fera </b>reacted diffently to the news. <br /> <br /> <b>Garou</b><br /> <br /> The werewolves are no longer a unified nation or even pretending to be such. <br /> <br /> The <b>Silver Fangs</b>, the <b>Shadow Lords</b>, the <b>Get of Fenris</b>, and the <b>Red Talons</b>, are weakly and unstablely allied. They mainly fight each other. They seek to rule humanity as kings. However, the long term side effects of the <b>Impergium </b>makes ruling human kingdoms amazingly tricky.<br /> <br /> The <b>Bone Gnawlers, </b>the <b>Glass Walkers</b>, the <b>Black Furies</b>, the <b>Fianna</b>, the <b>Children of Gaia, </b>\u200b\u200b\u200band the <b>Silent Striders</b>, have formed a council and rule themselves democratically. The <b>Garou Council </b>seeks to use their powers and spiritual connections to guide humanity in a healthy direction. They seek influence with the <b>Mages </b>and <b>Changelings </b>to move humanity in directions they prefer. <br /> <br /> The <b>Uktena </b>are seriously thinking of joining the Council. The main holdup is the fact the <b>Wendigo </b>don't want the <b>Uktena </b>to join. The <b>Wendigo </b>have made it clear that if the <b>Uktena </b>join the Council the <b>Wendigo </b>will disown them. Both native American tribes seek to guide their people to live in peace with the Earth. <b>\u200b\u200b</b>The <b>Uktena </b>don't see primitive technology and ancient tribal laws as absolute necessities. <br /> <br /> The <b>Stargazers </b>are in East Asia and not around in North America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-10-2026, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-28T18:21:02-07:00","id":1560247,"title":"","content":"<b>Ajaba: </b>These are know to still exist. But they stay in Africa and aren't in play.<br /> <br /> <b>Ananasi: </b>They are assumed to still be around laying low. Sightings in New Orleans are likely to be confirmed. <br /> <br /> <b>Bastet: </b>The breeds differ.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Bagheera: </i></b>Mainly in Asia but some are in North America. Some claim younger mages as apprentices. Older Mages generally negotiate but the apprentice relationship seems to work. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Balam: </i></b>Staying in South America mainly. Though Mexican Balam do wander in to some Mage communities explaining that they're joining the local Mage society. It gets accepted. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Bubasti: </i></b>Mainly in Egypt not actually noted outside of the Mediterranean basin area. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Ceilican: </i></b>Back and changed. They seem to have cut a deal with powerful Fay. They're known to be less fragile and more powerful. But they stay mainly in the British Isles and France. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Khan: </i></b>Mainly in Asia. They are in North America and they seem to be taking pointers from the Bagheera and Balam and asking to join Mage society as equal members. They make it clear they intend to try to shape human society in alliance with mages. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Pumonca: </i></b>Closely allied with the Wendigo. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Qualmi: </i></b>They are friendly with the Uktena, the Children of Gaia, and the Fianna. They seem to be interested in joining the Garou as members. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Simba: </i></b>They're mainly in Africa. There are a few scattered Simba beyond Africa. They mainly join other groups of Bastet. <br /> <br /> <b><i>Swara: </i></b>Mainly in Africa. <br /> <br /> To be Continued...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-28T18:32:25-07:00","id":1560248,"title":"","content":"<b>Corax: </b>They're everywhere crows are. Since mages seem to be the movers and shapers in this new society the Corax have asked for a seat at the table. They also make it clear that they are promoting alliances to shape the future in healthy ways. They aren't yet filling in their definition of &quot;Healthy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Gurahl: </b>The Werebears are working on setting up American Beast Courts like those in Asia. The Mages assume some of the Fera mean to join them, but the Gurahl plan to make the Mages join them.<br /> <br /> <b>Kitsume: </b>Mainly in Asia. However the foxes are in Hawaii and California as well. They seem to have plans. But it's hard to say what they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Mokole: </b>Strongly allied with the Werebears in setting up the American Beast Courts idea.<br /> <br /> <b>Nagah: </b>No one knows. This disturbs people.<br /> <br /> <b>Nuwisha: </b>Openly hostile to the Mages. They aren't killing people yet. They mainly challenge anything and everything the <b>Council of Traditions </b>tries to do. <br /> <br /> <b>Ratkin:</b> Violently hostile to humanity and determined to end all human civilization. They delight in spreading disease and famine. No other Fera are tolerant of the Ratkin.<br /> <br /> <b>Rokea:</b> They mainly keep to the seas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-28-2026, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-28T18:47:52-07:00","id":1560249,"title":"","content":"Lately a group of Sorcerers has undergone a transformation. This group was attempting to contact the Gaian spirit of the Owl. Their new totem turned them into owls. Now they've become Wereowls. <br /> <br /> Since their Warform looks vaguely like the cartoon character &quot;<b>\u200b\u200b\u200bOwl Jolson</b>&quot; this is seem as hilarious by the <b>Corax.</b> The Children of Gaia, the Fiana, the Gurahl, and the Corax, have received messages from Gaia to help the new tribe. <br /> <br /> With self deprecating humor the group is calling itself the <b>Owlins</b> after the Dungeons and Dragons creatures. <br /> <br /> Basically, the PCs could play as members of this group of Sorcerers trying to become Gaia's newest tribe. The politics and conflict their transformation would cause would be a lively way to use this setting for non mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}